('rowid-6713','GHBC-REQ-006713','GS 1207:2018',8,NULL,'8.22.3.1.4','GHBC-C-002125','The equivalent thickness of completely filled hollow concrete masonry is the actual thickness of the unit where loose-fill materials are: sand, pea gravel, crushed stone, or slag that meet ASTM C33 requirements; pumice, scoria, expanded shale, expanded clay, expanded slate, expanded slag, expanded fly ash, or cinders that comply with ASTM C331; or perlite or vermiculite meeting the requirements of ASTM C549 and ASTM C516, respectively.','material',NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,'[]','[]','[]',0.9,'extracted','VERIFIED','2018','341a0f69f38f6f767ad0040083716a079e15687ad06aa30575a0ad6cf7d14fc4','2026-08-15 13:56:13'),
